 "893e7fae-64e2-57b6-af19-e61e904ea8b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309829} {:answer/id #uuid "9e515d8a-f8c4-5ea9-9b59-674573d38b1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310026} {:answer/id #uuid "b92c0b6e-441f-5b77-9aa7-a8dc52625f53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04a488da-8074-50a9-ba1d-c7e0f32bf719" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308780} :answer-field/id #uuid "785b77fb-6634-5289-8f5e-c7972e2ca683" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "223e604f-882b-578c-9005-65a6a468f7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309006} {:answer/id #uuid "3a151fdc-c615-56f8-af30-2dacf342942e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309195} {:answer/id #uuid "7b511ce9-9c0e-54e8-8e7e-93916e342c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711} {:answer/id #uuid "ad26b27d-2be0-5935-829c-fe759d649c9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b511ce9-9c0e-54e8-8e7e-93916e342c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309711} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c99e1a2-52bb-5b04-85f5-ed344de385bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d36870f2-83c3-53eb-b9c4-cfdc50550717" :question/math-academy-id "q-335409" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this integral, we integrate by parts. \n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int {u}^{′}v\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=x,{u}^{′}=1,{v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and $v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2} & =\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c590c3-891b-511b-9e8d-1e0317eac036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309024} {:answer/id #uuid "c4250262-bc93-5a7e-a34a-2623ae9d7561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310322} {:answer/id #uuid "c82f0da4-6a92-5001-89a2-66f34618a0ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3/x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310355} {:answer/id #uuid "ee20a83a-6373-5864-bf59-eeaad3c5fb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4250262-bc93-5a7e-a34a-2623ae9d7561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310322} :answer-field/id #uuid "26833fad-1674-5264-a99a-1ab167ee5815" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34e87914-2491-5ea9-986c-2fa933b9f42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} {:answer/id #uuid "93802e8a-2438-526b-9013-756c85306841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309928} {:answer/id #uuid "cc68d1a8-cb75-5053-8d7d-c7bbccf33bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310385} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5f5849-731e-572b-9350-7951b8593415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}({e}^{x}+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34e87914-2491-5ea9-986c-2fa933b9f42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309150} :answer-field/id #uuid "842dfce6-3596-5e08-aa3d-f4ed3e02c6ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311159}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "039312c7-7497-5736-bf10-d497d1c61328" :question/math-academy-id "q-335412" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}\\cdot y & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{3})\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a701b78-2f7b-5869-a35c-a68265d84c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312297} {:answer/id #uuid "35b399dd-b281-56b7-8db7-a76855d06ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312408} {:answer/id #uuid "c01117c8-2cdb-582a-8d44-4d6c98807eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313480} {:answer/id #uuid "e4465b0a-93ed-52f4-b50c-bf89f91e8717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4465b0a-93ed-52f4-b50c-bf89f91e8717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313777} :answer-field/id #uuid "619b5a02-9bcf-5c4e-9804-90020e919aba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8ab38f-ccc9-5c4d-9953-e2511696a304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312314} {:answer/id #uuid "82438980-e317-5426-8c57-7d992347312f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313024} {:answer/id #uuid "a83c841e-df51-5c6e-b081-e26fb120e44e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313294} {:answer/id #uuid "ab3cf1a5-b0c2-595f-a092-5ea9a23fd911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82438980-e317-5426-8c57-7d992347312f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313024} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5afcbd6-0c6a-5f61-91f9-74372beb0557" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314457}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f406ffe6-dbd4-575f-96ea-c90a9a6d9f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-339140" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y=7,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{5}{x}$ and $Q(x)=7.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (5/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5})} \\\\  & ={x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{5}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y) & ={x}^{5}\\cdot 7 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{x}^{4}y & =7{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{5})\\,dx & =\\int 7{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd0b65e-3a0f-5994-9689-9aef5b5c9454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{-x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391570} {:answer/id #uuid "3fae5784-6514-5371-820c-1909539d4c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391571} {:answer/id #uuid "58c34fda-7cad-508d-a7f2-d8bf06c08b7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391572} {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7448e8d2-a22f-59f6-bc6b-c65f6e7cf2de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391573} :answer-field/id #uuid "d308949f-707a-5a2c-802c-a0a17c33433a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4e6cf3c-fccb-5029-b604-d1593b0daddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391575} {:answer/id #uuid "1e61f74a-48e8-542c-a33f-c9fe7a376f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391576} {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} {:answer/id #uuid "fb69fbee-2b0a-5d6f-b11d-267cf756dd9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74653977-5fc1-57a5-a3e9-24eb70eb33c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391577} :answer-field/id #uuid "2021aa17-0151-5e2d-987a-a1856edc5e53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391574}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6530e5db-b521-5f5c-99f7-59872d852e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-335402" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=6{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is already in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=6{e}^{2x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot 6{e}^{2x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =6{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =6{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =-6{e}^{-x}+C \\\\ y & =-6{e}^{2x}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d5e5efa-0ad9-5cb1-8007-def75d4c0f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391733} {:answer/id #uuid "181ce215-60ee-5a98-8d16-1f87a5c66bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391734} {:answer/id #uuid "c201762a-3b3f-52e3-a4c2-6f449ab4bd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391735} {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45bdee38-54f6-5e18-9b5f-1f916081c4c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391736} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52979ca-88b2-53be-b424-0a20f99bf0c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02bcb740-d3b0-5e03-ac52-deeb78de3ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391738} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0496f9-803e-5f66-af97-d84ac1ef5ec2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391739} {:answer/id #uuid "917a7312-27b6-560b-80be-1afb23076cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391740} {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94fc55df-9a81-5694-9adb-ccac511991c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391741} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e39085e-c8a9-5cbc-b6d2-646a14b27243" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391737}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08d92346-a7e8-58c6-8d60-e4702d743dd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-339138" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=x{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=-3$ and $Q(x)=x{e}^{3x}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int -3\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={e}^{-3x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y) & ={e}^{-3x}\\cdot x{e}^{3x} \\\\ {e}^{-3x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{e}^{-3x}\\cdot y & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x}) & =x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{-3x})\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{-3x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435866 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435836} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb32a9a-ce7c-5dfe-90c1-5f241762ceee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435842} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf9a5e7-9387-5f18-9a2c-3d8174e2d646" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435852} {:answer/id #uuid "f669873b-95d4-589e-957f-2bb522268738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21b04f8f-b31f-5e1d-8a4e-18caced2e9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435836} :answer-field/id #uuid "054a463e-8111-5ef5-af3f-4d0babd67edf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435840} {:answer/id #uuid "96612919-8760-51a3-a0ec-f59a5ea738c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435844} {:answer/id #uuid "a91ab2dc-5a5e-503c-8f55-0ebae59165d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435848} {:answer/id #uuid "cceac854-6bb0-51ac-8a27-c1be3b7727f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "856f41fb-43dc-578b-9457-c64453f94455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435840} :answer-field/id #uuid "658b2e4e-a8cb-5de8-9ced-3ee2b6b96997" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435862}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "536cae39-f031-5c30-a8b0-a9b62b8632a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339139" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y=5,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=5.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot 5 \\\\ {x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}y & =5{x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int 5{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & ={x}^{5}+C \\\\ y & =x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577953 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e86e3f8-835a-5e7b-800f-ceabc4489397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577958} {:answer/id #uuid "3120bb10-b47c-5419-8adb-97f2655124d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577959} {:answer/id #uuid "a1417d20-4b8d-5020-96a5-2fbfbd7050c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577987} {:answer/id #uuid "b83df480-6b6b-5335-b4e1-f7290ebda4f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1417d20-4b8d-5020-96a5-2fbfbd7050c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577987} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab4e553-4d18-5597-a3e0-73deea59b791" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3570ef95-2759-5e30-953f-28e1ebb98a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{3 x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577960} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfccc74-2fa7-5b51-a206-88395113b5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{6 x}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577968} {:answer/id #uuid "7331aa7a-74a0-5dd6-9a77-f5c139e3cdc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{6 x}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577975} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb021b5-ba70-5bfd-8dc9-a93c7df005cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{3 x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb021b5-ba70-5bfd-8dc9-a93c7df005cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{3 x}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577984} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc886d9b-0870-5428-8a5d-36eef483e7f9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577991}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16f4ba5c-38ec-56ab-af32-6a47ecbd1681" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{3}{x}y = 6, x > 0$.\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe general solution is given by $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{3}{x}$ and $Q(x)=6.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (3/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{x}y) & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 6 \\\\ {x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}y & =6{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{3})\\,dx & =\\int 6{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{3} & =\\frac{6{x}^{4}}{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x}{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12ff3b91-e441-53af-9062-6172c2b943f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577952} {:answer/id #uuid "373e6e78-bb4e-5bed-a8e8-55dacc8ccc10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577961} {:answer/id #uuid "7397983b-bc5c-5274-811c-59b5f13c7eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577977} {:answer/id #uuid "81f61c18-c835-5e8a-9d3e-f07e5752fa7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "373e6e78-bb4e-5bed-a8e8-55dacc8ccc10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577961} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0d1af8b-2f60-532b-833e-d252be943f4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f050ba8-39e0-5be7-9ece-a578463cd06e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{e^{x}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577962} {:answer/id #uuid "70463e2d-dbe2-52a4-8bbd-dcc9506cd406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} - \\frac{e^{x}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577973} {:answer/id #uuid "89ef23a5-a7af-51fe-891d-0e42cd073f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} + \\frac{e^{x}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577983} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f13012-e3ee-5f3b-93fe-73810dc6f26f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{3}} - \\frac{e^{x}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186578002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f050ba8-39e0-5be7-9ece-a578463cd06e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{x^{4}} + \\frac{e^{x}}{x^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577962} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd0c018f-ca74-55e5-bd9c-88c330a1225e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "61d6ddc4-7ed9-5f0f-ab2d-6fc07bf6c3bb" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{4}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{4}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{4}}.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (4/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{4}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{4}{x}y) & ={x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{x}^{3}\\cdot y & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{4})\\,dx & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{4} & ={e}^{x}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+C}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186578001 :question/answer-